  "answer": "I'll start by inspecting the workspace and the relevant files.\nThe bug is clear: `add` subtracts instead of adding. Let me fix it and check the runtime.\nDone — addition is repaired.\n\n## What was wrong\n`src/add.ts` implemented `add` with subtraction:\n\n```ts\nexport function add(a: number, b: number) { return a - b }\n```\n\n## The fix\nReplaced the operator only — the exported name, both `number` parameters, and the inferred `number` return type are unchanged:\n\n```ts\nexport function add(a: number, b: number) { return a + b }\n```\n\n## Verification\nRan the existing test runner (Bun, as required by the `bun:test` import) with no added config and no changes to the test:\n\n```\nbun test v1.3.14\ntest/oracle.test.ts:\n(pass) addition across signed inputs [0.14ms]\n\n 1 pass\n 0 fail\n 5 expect() calls\n```\n\nAll five cases pass, including the ones that distinguish the operators: negatives (`-5 + -7 = -12`), a negative first operand (`-2 + 3 = 1`), zeros, and a carry across a place boundary (`99 + 1 = 100`).\n\n`AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` were left untouched, and no files were added to the workspace."
